    "faq": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q-1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is NAD+ and why is it important?",
            "answer": "<p>NAD+ (nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide) is a coenzyme naturally found in every living cell in your body. It plays an essential role in converting nutrients into energy, supporting cellular metabolism and helping maintain healthy cellular function. NAD+ is also involved in DNA repair.</p>",
            "open": true
          }
        },
        "q-2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What are the benefits of NAD+ supplements?",
            "answer": "<p>NAD+ supplements are attracting interest for their potential role in cellular energy and healthy aging. Research into NAD+ and its precursors is growing, with encouraging findings in laboratory studies and certain human trials. However, scientists are still investigating how supplementation affects everyday energy, physical performance and long-term health.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q-4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does it take to notice results?",
            "answer": "<p>Everyone's experience may be different. Some people may notice no obvious changes at all, even if certain biological markers change. Research into NAD+ precursors has demonstrated measurable changes in NAD-related levels over weeks, but there is no established timeline for noticeable improvements in energy or well-being.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q-5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is NAD+ suitable for everyday use?",
            "answer": "<p>Several human studies of NAD+ precursors have reported generally good tolerability over weeks to months. However, long-term safety information remains limited, and the findings depend on the specific ingredient and dose. Always follow the product's directions, and consult a healthcare professional if you're pregnant, breastfeeding, taking medication or managing a medical condition.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q-6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How many capsules come in each bottle?",
            "answer": "<p>Each bottle contains 30 capsules, designed to fit conveniently into your daily routine. Please refer to the product's recommended serving size and directions for use.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q-7": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I combine NAD+ with my other supplements?",
            "answer": "<p>Your supplement routine should work for your individual needs. Check the full ingredient list to avoid taking overlapping ingredients, especially if you already use other NAD+ or vitamin B3 products. Your pharmacist or healthcare professional can help identify potential interactions with medications or other supplements.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q-resveratrol-pair": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why is resveratrol paired with NAD+?",
            "answer": "<p>Resveratrol has been studied for how it interacts with sirtuins, a family of proteins that depend on NAD+ to work. That connection is why the two are often taken together.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q-resveratrol-what": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is resveratrol?",
            "answer": "<p>Resveratrol is a natural compound found in grape skins, red wine, peanuts and some berries. It's a polyphenol, a type of antioxidant that plants produce to protect themselves.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "q-resveratrol-safe": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is resveratrol safe to take every day?",
            "answer": "<p>In human studies, resveratrol has generally been well tolerated at common supplement doses, though higher doses have been linked to stomach upset in some people.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        }
      },
